Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["WedgeCoeff", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1153,ExpressionUUID->"846e2898-34c7-491d-ae2a-cdfaacb58aed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"5efc04e7-b2b0-4d9c-baa6-10b180294c35"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["WedgeCoeff"]], 
     "paclet:VasilDimitrov/SolutionsX/ref/WedgeCoeff", 
     "VasilDimitrov Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["sol", "TI"], "]", "[", 
   StyleBox["expr", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "71ce3ef3-6a90-445f-8653-6b572fe1b5eb"],
 "\[LineSeparator]extracts the antisymmetric component tensor of a form \
written in wedges of coordinate differentials, as the lowest-rank equivalent: \
a form of degree p above half the dimension d is Hodge-dualized and expanded \
first, and the extraction runs on the dual, giving the component tensor of \
the Hodge dual with d-p free indices.\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"2e13d386-a5c9-4e75-b720-2d509c399032"],
 "For p at most d/2 the result is the plain component tensor, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["WedgeCoeff"]], 
    "paclet:VasilDimitrov/SolutionsX/ref/WedgeCoeff", 
    "VasilDimitrov Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "cf30e854-720f-48bc-91d7-dac6460e11d2"],
 " inverts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ExpandForms"]], 
    "paclet:VasilDimitrov/SolutionsX/ref/ExpandForms", 
    "VasilDimitrov Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "1cb54c8b-35c1-43d0-88a2-606a9b3a43cb"],
 ": the companion tensor comes back exactly.\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"d9501d57-9b9d-4e0c-97c0-90fa82102dee"],
 "Reconstructing a dualized form from its result costs the double-dual sign \
(-1)^(p(d-p)) sign(det g) \[LongDash] in Lorentzian signature the volume form \
extracts to minus its coefficient. That sign is mathematics, not a \
convention.\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"296f8bfa-3c86-4c8d-b6a4-2fc74035221b"],
 "The result is presented in the order of the manifold's Index list: the \
frees introduced by the extraction take the first names not already free in \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["expr", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "8c8b4c30-b25d-453d-bb6e-677b212fe445"],
 ", and ScreenDollarIndices renames the dummies to the following unused ones. \
If the registered list is exhausted mid-extraction, new indices are generated \
and registered, so the extraction always succeeds.\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"80ba44bb-a486-4fbc-9bfa-cb2c0b603640"],
 "Only ContractMetric is applied to the result; simplification is left to the \
caller."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->1154,ExpressionUUID->"b5af539a-69b0-4947-ad7f-0fb0c1ba020c"],

Cell["\<\
WedgeCoeff[sol][expr] reads off the antisymmetric component tensor of a form \
written in wedges of coordinate differentials, by replacing each wedge \
monomial with antisymmetrized products of deltas: the form evaluated on \
coordinate vector fields.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1155,ExpressionUUID->"3345fbda-b0d3-4aeb-b321-befc4a2806cd"],

Cell["\<\
The lowest-rank equivalent is returned: above half the manifold dimension the \
expression is Hodge-dualized and expanded first \[LongDash] the star trick, \
performed as an actual Hodge operation \[LongDash] so a d-form gives a \
scalar, a (d-1)-form one free index, and in general d-p of them; the result \
is the component tensor of the Hodge dual of the form.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1156,ExpressionUUID->"e13d1fa7-4ed6-4d09-a7e9-ce9b421b8663"],

Cell["\<\
Reconstructing a dualized form from its result costs the double-dual sign \
(-1)^(p(d-p)) sign(det g): in Lorentzian signature the volume form extracts \
to minus its coefficient. That sign is mathematics, not a convention.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1157,ExpressionUUID->"60029374-4805-4132-a545-86a18c546a26"],

Cell["\<\
At degree p at most d/2 no epsilon is involved and WedgeCoeff inverts \
ExpandForms: applied to an expanded form it returns the companion tensor \
exactly.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1158,ExpressionUUID->"8e874534-ea3c-49d8-aa42-cfaa87e6eb6c"],

Cell["\<\
The result is presented in the order of the manifold's Index list: the frees \
introduced by the extraction take the first names not already free in expr, \
and ScreenDollarIndices renames the dummies to the following unused ones. If \
the registered list is exhausted mid-extraction, new indices are generated \
and registered, so the extraction always succeeds.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1159,ExpressionUUID->"57288859-f26f-4bde-88f2-c22fb6956f51"],

Cell["\<\
Downstairs coordinate differentials are first raised through the metric; \
ambiguities follow the take-the-first convention (first manifold, first \
metric).\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1160,ExpressionUUID->"6f012b55-1bcd-4043-836d-31bfd5cc5f2c"],

Cell["\<\
The expression must be homogeneous in degree; Hodge duals appearing in it are \
expanded internally, while any other content that is not a wedge of \
coordinate differentials is refused with a message.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1161,ExpressionUUID->"c589f036-3196-4742-b356-8db575692a25"],

Cell["\<\
Only ContractMetric is applied to the result; simplification is left to the \
caller.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1162,ExpressionUUID->"2fc69efc-3ac0-4a90-b035-fdd5771d2c4b"],

Cell["WedgeCoeff has the attribute HoldFirst.", "Notes",
 CellID->1163,ExpressionUUID->"e74f8249-e396-4277-aa9f-684c062d09a8"]
}, Open  ]],

